 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S442-016\", \"clauses\": {\"illustrate\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"Shade {fraction_str} of the shape.\", \"reasoning\": \"F17 asks the learner to shade part of a shape, which is the illustrate task. Its fraction_str is nested from F08 (numerator 1 over denominator 2 or 4), which gives the two fractions this lc names.\"}, \"half\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"Shade {fraction_str} of the shape.\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 with numerator 1 and denominator 2 prints 1/2 as fraction_str, and F17 shows it as a shaded shape.\"}, \"quarter\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"Shade {fraction_str} of the shape.\", \"reasoning\": \"F08 with numerator 1 and denominator 4 prints 1/4 as fraction_str, and F17 shows it as a shaded shape.\"}, \"parts_of_whole\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F04\", \"template\": \"A {frac_lbl} shows how many equal parts are shaded out of the total.\", \"reasoning\": \"F04 states the part-of-a-whole idea using equal parts and the total. frac_lbl is the word fraction, which this lc introduces, and every word of the sentence is in cumulative_vocab or introduces_vocab.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F06\", \"F07\", \"F16\", \"F17\", \"F21\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"The {den_lbl} (bottom number) tells the total equal parts: {den}.\", \"The {num_lbl} (top number) tells how many parts are taken: {num}.\", \"{unshaded}/{denom}\", \"Shade {fraction_str} of the shape.\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 and F07 print the gate word in the slot and then repeat it in parentheses. The gate always prints bottom number for denominator and top number for numerator for this lc, so every render shows the same phrase twice, which is misleading wording for a grade 1 learner. F21 (template {unshaded}/{denom}) is nested in F17. Its unshaded slot is denominator minus numerator, so with denominator 4 and numerator 1 it prints 3/4. That is a fraction the lc does not name and is not a unit fraction, despite the declared unit_fraction bound, so F21 and F17 (the question text that carries it) are outside scope. F16 (template {unshaded}/{denom}) is a distractor in distractors and format_data.mcq_options. With denominator 2 and numerator 1, its unshaded slot is 1, so it can print 1/2, the same value as the keyed answer, and nothing in the packet shows the generator removes that duplicate. The F11 set model and number line names were considered and not failed: the packet does not show they are outside parts of a whole.\"}",
